# Trivy IaC allowlist for this repo.
#
# Each entry below was manually reviewed. These are not oversights - they
# are consequences of explicit, documented cost/architecture tradeoffs
# elsewhere in this lab (see README's "Cloud security" section). Do not add
# entries here without reviewing the actual finding first.

# AVD-AWS-0104: Security groups allow unrestricted egress (0.0.0.0/0).
# Accepted: both VMs need outbound internet access (apt updates, Docker
# image pulls, curl-based installs, git clone of the Wazuh Docker repo) and
# there is deliberately no NAT Gateway (cost tradeoff for a short-lived
# evaluation lab). Ingress is what actually matters for exposure, and it is
# tightly restricted: the App VM only accepts SSH/HTTPS from an evaluator IP
# allowlist plus a crypto-authenticated WireGuard port, and the Wazuh VM
# accepts nothing from the internet at all - every one of its ingress rules
# references the App security group by ID, not a CIDR block.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AVD-AWS-0164: Public subnet auto-assigns public IPs to instances.
# Accepted: for the same NAT Gateway cost-avoidance reason above, both VMs
# need a public IP purely to reach the internet outbound. This does not
# translate into inbound exposure - that's controlled entirely by security
# group rules (see AVD-AWS-0104 note above), not by subnet routing.
AVD-AWS-0164
